From f91952805c80409c1491d2708713b264fa8f5862 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 17:58:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] usb: device: expose a transfer slot's work item for
 diagnostics
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Lets an out-of-band watchdog inspect the raw k_work state (flags, owning
queue, pending-list membership) of a transfer whose completion appears
never to run — the state every captured CDC wedge ends in on Telink B91.

Signed-off-by: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
---
 subsys/usb/device/usb_transfer.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/subsys/usb/device/usb_transfer.c b/subsys/usb/device/usb_transfer.c
index 47b4111b2..0e24995d2 100644
--- a/subsys/usb/device/usb_transfer.c
+++ b/subsys/usb/device/usb_transfer.c
@@ -334,6 +334,20 @@ size_t usb_transfer_slots_snapshot(uint8_t *eps, int8_t *statuses,
 	return n;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Diagnostic access to a slot's work item, so an out-of-band watchdog can
+ * inspect the raw k_work state (flags, owning queue, list membership) of a
+ * transfer whose completion appears never to run.
+ */
+struct k_work *usb_transfer_slot_work(size_t idx)
+{
+	if (idx >= ARRAY_SIZE(ut_data)) {
+		return NULL;
+	}
+
+	return &ut_data[idx].work;
+}
+
 /*
  * Mark a live transfer canceled and hand it to the workqueue for completion.
  * If the submission is refused (queue tearing down, item already mid-cancel)
-- 
2.53.0

